{
  "id": "ep059",
  "duration": 45.155,
  "beats": [
    {
      "start": 0.08,
      "end": 4.476,
      "text": "Astronauts floating in orbit are actually not beyond Earth's gravity.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS-134 International Space Station after undocking.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS-134_International_Space_Station_after_undocking.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.367,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 2.367,
          "end": 4.467,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 4.476,
      "end": 10.996,
      "text": "While many believe space is a complete zero gravity vacuum, the everyday reality is quite different.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "A Horseshoe Einstein Ring from Hubble.JPG",
        "credit": "Lensshoe_hubble.jpg: ESA/Hubble & NASA\nderivative work: Bulwersator (talk)",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:A_Horseshoe_Einstein_Ring_from_Hubble.JPG"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 4.467,
          "end": 11.0,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 10.996,
      "end": 19.116,
      "text": "At the soaring altitude of the space station, Earth's gravitational field is still nearly 90 percent as strong as on the ground.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "designed card"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 11.0,
          "end": 19.1,
          "kind": "designed",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 19.116,
      "end": 25.536,
      "text": "Human space travellers do not float because gravity has vanished entirely from their location.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "NASA astronaut Nichole Ayers conducts research operations inside the Life Science Glovebox (iss073e0118821).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA Johnson Space Center",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:NASA_astronaut_Nichole_Ayers_conducts_research_operations_inside_the_Life_Science_Glovebox_(iss073e0118821).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 19.1,
          "end": 22.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 22.167,
          "end": 25.533,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 25.536,
      "end": 31.281,
      "text": "Instead, they stay up because they are caught in a continuous state of perpetual free fall.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Newton's cannonball cropped.png",
        "credit": "Isaac Newton",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Newton%27s_cannonball_cropped.png"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 25.533,
          "end": 29.5,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        },
        {
          "start": 29.5,
          "end": 31.267,
          "kind": "detail",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 31.281,
      "end": 37.826,
      "text": "Their immense horizontal speed continually carries them around the curving horizon of our home planet.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "Lucy Earth Gravity Assist 2 Trajectory Visualizations (SVS5429 - lucy ega2 pov-full 02400 print).jpg",
        "credit": "NASA's Scientific Visualization Studio - USRA/Kel Elkins, KBR Wyle Services, LLC/Dan Gallagher, SwRI/Katherine Kretke",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lucy_Earth_Gravity_Assist_2_Trajectory_Visualizations_(SVS5429_-_lucy_ega2_pov-full_02400_print).jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 31.267,
          "end": 37.833,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "start": 37.826,
      "end": 44.805,
      "text": "That precise physics mechanism is why astronauts floating in orbit are actually not beyond Earth's gravity.",
      "asset": {
        "source": "Wikimedia Commons",
        "title": "STS-134 International Space Station after undocking.jpg",
        "credit": "NASA",
        "license": "Public domain",
        "url": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:STS-134_International_Space_Station_after_undocking.jpg"
      },
      "shots": [
        {
          "start": 37.833,
          "end": 45.167,
          "kind": "card",
          "motion": "camera"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
